## Context

Adopted framing: conception/jetp-short-paper-framing-2026-09-15.md.
Which components of a just transition progress within JETPs, with which public
and private finance, and from which pre-existing operations?
Acceleration is the motivating question; the observed financial and operation
histories delimit the empirical answer. Parent programme: 0725.
Earlier causal-only acceptance criteria are superseded by the author's adopted
descriptive study. Historical decisions remain in Git and the feasibility notes.

## First documentary acceptance check

Trace the central sentence and each figure panel to the frozen 0730 run.
If panels use different samples, their labels and claims must expose that fact.
A stage difference cannot be described as speed or causal acceleration; a
documentary gap cannot be described as an actual absence of private finance.

## Actions

Write the short manuscript in deliverables/jetp-mesure using 0711, with one
dominant finding supported by the other two dimensions in 0823. Explain the
contribution relative to published JETP research and retain contrary evidence.
Discuss transition functions, the documented social objectives and beneficiaries,
public/private instruments, and pre-existing project histories. Distinguish
funding objectives from realised justice outcomes and association from catalysis.

Replace the old disbursement-only conception framing with reproducible results.
Do not predetermine instrument substitution or failure. The data paper describes
infrastructure; this short paper establishes the substantive empirical finding.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Question and contribution implement the adopted framing and frozen protocol
- [ ] Literature comparison explains what the empirical result adds or revises
- [ ] Three dimensions support one coherent argument with sample limits explicit
- [ ] Central figure and all quantitative claims reproduce from pinned outputs
- [ ] Social objectives, physical outcomes and financial milestones remain distinct
- [ ] Null/mixed findings, missingness and sensitivities reported
- [ ] LaTeX manuscript builds with resolved sources and is ready for review

